course: dictionary
lesson: 13884
title: Knowledgeable
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A knowledgeable person knows a lot about something, or about many things. «The guide at the museum was knowledgeable about dinosaurs.» The guide knew many facts about dinosaurs, so you could trust what they told you.
explain: Knowledgeable often comes with the word about, as in «knowledgeable about plants». It tells you whom to ask when you have a question. If you want to learn about the stars, ask someone who is knowledgeable about space.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «Ask Mrs Patel, she is knowledgeable about plants.» The words ask and plants tell you that Mrs Patel knows a lot about plants, so she is the person to go to with your garden questions.
fact: Knowledgeable means knowing a lot about something, or about many things.
fact: Knowledgeable is an adjective, so it describes a person or thing, as in «a knowledgeable guide».
fact: The adverb is knowledgeably, as in «She spoke knowledgeably about rivers».
fact: Knowledgeable is often followed by about, as in «knowledgeable about dinosaurs».
fact: Knowledgeable is a close friend of the word knowledge, which means what you know.
exercise: «The museum guide was knowledgeable about dinosaurs.» What does knowledgeable mean? | Keen to go home early | *Knowing a lot about something | Very tired after a long walk | Frightened of big animals
exercise: «Ask Mrs Patel, she is knowledgeable about plants.» Who should you ask about plants? | The dog next door | *Mrs Patel | Nobody, plants cannot be learned about | The bus driver
exercise: «Sam is knowledgeable about space, and he knows the names of all the planets.» Find and copy one word that means knowing a lot. | *knowledgeable | space | Sam | planets
test: «Sam is knowledgeable about space.» What does this tell us about Sam? | He cannot find his shoes | *He knows a lot about space | He has never seen a star | He is afraid of the dark
test: What is the adverb form of knowledgeable? | knowledgeable | *knowledgeably | knowing | knowledge
exam: Which sentence uses knowledgeable correctly? | The rain was very knowledgeable | The door was knowledgeable and shut quickly | *The teacher was knowledgeable about rivers and mountains | I ate a knowledgeable sandwich
